, `C_inter`, and `C_dir` close the family of graphs under nonempty intersections and directed unions, and `funSpaceReprIso` is Exercise 3.27. `sierpinski`, `mapOfOpen`, `openOfMap`, and `openIso` identify open sets of elements with approximable maps into the Sierpiński domain, and `opensReprIso` transports that to function-space elements. **Theorem:** partial — the product identities of 3.1–3.7 and the function-space results 3.10–3.13 and 3.27 are proved, but the isomorphic disjoint copy of \(\mathcal{D}_1\) is not constructed and no stem defines a functor. **Proof:** partial — the arguments are the padding, preimage, and round-trip comparisons just named, while the opening’s generality claim has no proof in the closure.
